WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.628
Today, September sixth, twenty twenty-six, we are introducing the beta of EMOS:
the Enterprise Modernization Operating System.

00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:11.237
This release establishes a decision-intelligence foundation for continuous
enterprise modernization.

00:00:12.758 --> 00:00:18.678
Imagine a global aerospace and manufacturing enterprise, comparable in scale and
complexity to industry leaders such as Boeing.

00:00:18.978 --> 00:00:28.518
This is an illustrative scenario, not a claim about Boeing: more than five
thousand internal and external digital products support engineering, factories,
supply chains, employees, partners, and customers.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:35.797
Over decades, critical products accumulate aging runtimes, databases,
infrastructure, and undocumented dependencies.

00:00:36.097 --> 00:00:44.234
Licensing and operating costs rise. Teams spend more time sustaining the estate,
while new business initiatives wait for products that can no longer change safely
or quickly.

00:00:45.758 --> 00:00:47.912
The question is no longer whether to modernize.

00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:54.019
When thousands of products need attention, how do you decide what to modernize,
what to preserve, what to replace, and where to begin?

00:00:55.550 --> 00:01:04.699
The complete journey begins with business intent, then discovers the estate,
understands evidence, assesses options, makes governed decisions, plans investment
and delivery waves, and mobilizes teams.

00:01:04.999 --> 00:01:14.391
Execution, validation, benefit measurement, learning, and continuous reassessment
complete the loop. Business, architecture, security, finance, and delivery each
contribute evidence and decisions.

00:01:15.925 --> 00:01:21.898
EMOS envisions one operating system connecting enterprise evidence, explainable
modernization decisions, and program planning.

00:01:22.198 --> 00:01:28.252
The aim is a shared, continuously improving view of every workload, the evidence
behind each choice, and the governed journey that follows.

00:01:29.758 --> 00:01:38.888
The beta implements a focused vertical slice from program alignment and portfolio
discovery through Enterprise DNA, six-R assessment, explainable decisions, wave
planning, and mobilization readiness.

00:01:39.188 --> 00:01:45.663
It does not execute migrations, provision landing zones, staff delivery teams, or
claim live CMDB and cloud-agent discovery.

00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:51.900
Users can explore representative workloads or bring their own portfolio through
CSV or JSON.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:02:00.103
EMOS validates the inventory, protects against formula injection, shows valid and
invalid rows, and converts incomplete fields into visible evidence gaps instead of
hiding them.

00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:08.811
For Customer Analytics, EMOS structures eighteen attributes across Business,
Technology, Dependency, Economics, Data and Risk, and Target-State DNA.

00:02:09.111 --> 00:02:15.737
Eleven attributes are verified, one is incomplete, and six are missing, producing
a deterministic evidence-completeness score of sixty-one percent.

00:02:17.258 --> 00:02:25.204
The structured evidence passes into the Gemini reasoning pipeline and the
canonical six-R framework: Retain, Retire, Rehost, Replatform, Refactor, or
Repurchase.

00:02:25.504 --> 00:02:36.280
The result explains its recommendation, alternatives, risks, assumptions, evidence
gaps, and next actions. Model confidence and deterministic completeness remain
distinct, while readiness stays Needs Evidence when critical facts are missing.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.511
A decision is not frozen in time.

00:02:39.811 --> 00:02:47.199
Architects can add verified evidence, preserve the assessment history, and revisit
the recommendation as dependencies, constraints, and enterprise standards become
clearer.

00:02:48.717 --> 00:02:53.441
Governed decisions then move into program alignment, deterministic wave planning,
and mobilization readiness.

00:02:53.741 --> 00:03:02.948
Sponsors, owners, outcomes, platform strategy, security, people, delivery, and
open evidence gates remain visible. The Executive Pack turns that context into a
portable decision artifact.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:10.951
The beta uses a React and TypeScript experience with Tailwind CSS and Vite, backed
by Node.js and Express on Google Cloud Run.

00:03:11.251 --> 00:03:24.903
Firebase Authentication provides Google sign-in. Cloud Firestore stores owner-
bound portfolios, assessments, conversations, and program context. Google Secret
Manager protects server credentials. Gemini three point six Flash is the primary
model, supported by a resilient fallback ladder.

00:03:26.425 --> 00:03:29.242
This beta does not deploy autonomous agents or subagents.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:37.988
It uses one governed Gemini decision pipeline with deterministic evidence scoring,
prompt fencing, secret redaction, vendor-neutral reasoning, taxonomy enforcement,
and readiness checks.

00:03:38.288 --> 00:03:48.473
The roadmap proposes Google ADK specialist agents for risk and governance,
business value, target architecture, wave planning, execution, and validation,
with human approval gates and agent-to-agent interoperability.

00:03:50.008 --> 00:03:53.676
Marketplace distribution is a planned direction, not a current listing or
approval.

00:03:53.976 --> 00:04:02.167
The intended path starts with Google Cloud Marketplace, then evaluates other
hyperscaler marketplaces and relevant agentic-AI marketplaces as the product and
governance model mature.

00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:08.400
Modernization starts with knowing what you have, understanding what matters, and
making decisions you can explain.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:15.782
Explore the EMOS beta, inspect a workload's evidence, generate a recommendation,
and help shape the operating system for continuous enterprise modernization.
